hey guys i am katherine mccourt i'm so  excited that we're here today because  this is pro tips from pro  chefs  i am the founder of welicious m1 potato  and i'm going to be sharing  a recipe i absolutely love there are a  ton of different tips involved in this  one  it is healthy delicious really easy  only one piece of equipment that's the  airfryer we're  making vegetables in an airfryer aka air  fried veggies the best part about it  no matter the season whether you're at  the farmer's market or the grocery  you can take any kind of vegetables and  use it in  this recipe but if you are in the winter  you could use  winter squash you could use pumpkins  again carrots  onions like the world is your oyster  if you're used to roasting vegetables  forget it it is  all about air frying them to start  again just grabbing like any of your  favorite vegetables  just give them a good little wash and  the trick to this is you want to make  sure to cut them  in even sized pieces but you can see  that like out sometimes i'll even just  pull these little florets just like this  because sometimes i like little ones and  i like bigger pieces  uh and so that's all we're doing with  the cauliflower and like  make it wild and crazy grab purple  cauliflower yellow white  like it's fun to get a bunch of  different vegetables  because that's where you're going to get  this really vibrant assortment  so now i've got the little patty pan  squash and i'll just cut them  right in half just like that and then  this one is a little bit bigger  so i'll take off the top just pull off  that little stem i'm going to put that  to the side  um and then we're just going to quarter  these and they get  really like crispy on the outside super  tender inside and then like i said like  see how this chunk  is very similar we ordered that one  they're about even sized  and then a carrot so you think of like a  carrot really  hard crunchy but when it's in an air  fryer it's just gonna get like  really tender and the natural sweetness  from the carrot gets caramelized and it  is like  next level i just cut these into batons  but you could also cut them into  coins like big coins if you want um you  know what let's go wild and crazy let's  let's cut a few coins and we'll  cut a few batons and this is a great way  like look if you guys have kids  get your kids in pull in a board um you  know  summer time give them a kids safe knife  and let them help cut vegetables  that's a great way to get them to kind  of snack on them at the same time  look at that all colors textures shapes  sizes and what we're going to do is just  open the airfryer right up and put this  in i'm going to actually pull out my  basket because this is one of those pro  tips i've been talking about  so you have your empty air fryer right  here  and i'm just going to take my vegetables  and put them right in  what i love about this is that we don't  even have to get  another bowl out uh to wash and have to  deal with and clean because  your airfryer basket is gonna act as  your bowl  so go ahead and this is another pro tip  i love to take a spray  so you could use olive oil canola oil  ghee spray  that i've got here anything because  what's great about the spray  is that it evenly just kind of kisses  each  nook and cranny of the vegetables so  it's going to get these like nice  golden bits making them really crispy on  the outside  but soft and tender inside so then we're  going to take a little bit of salt  i like to do some kosher salt here but  you could also get in some pepper  open up your spice drawer do not ignore  your spice drawer this is the time to  pull out like  some cumin some curry garam masala  any kind of like spices that you've been  like dying  um to play around with this is the time  to use them  now i just give it a little bit of a  shake so put it right in the air fryer  click it on air fry we're gonna we're  gonna  actually turn the temperature down with  vegetables i like to do  somewhere between 375 and 400 today  we're going to go like 400  um and go any you know this is one thing  that you want to just keep an eye on i  like to do 20 minutes especially for  cauliflower and carrots they're a little  bit harder we want to make them more  tender  so go ahead and give it a little bit of  time you may need to pull out some  vegetables  a little bit earlier than others it  makes a delicious side  you could make in an entree by putting a  little bit of hummus on the side one of  my favorite summertime recipes  is to take my air fried vegetables with  lettuce like really nice crunchy lettuce  a nice vinaigrette and you're gonna have  an air fried vegetable salad  that will make anyone in your life crazy  happy belly's filled healthy delicious  and really easy again i'm katherine  mccord you can find me  licious at one potato box and if you  make this recipe which i hope you do  don't forget to share it on at drew  barramore show  and hashtag drew barramore show so we  can find what you're making in your  kitchen this summer
 

